course: dictionary
lesson: 11454
title: The adjudicator
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a job. Look at the words around them to find out what the job is. «The adjudicator listened to every singer, then picked the winner.» Singers, a winner and listening are clues: an adjudicator is the person who judges.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «The adjudicator gave each team a score.» If you swap in judge, the sentence still makes sense, so an adjudicator is a judge.
explain: Adjudicator is a formal word. «The adjudicator decided that the two neighbours should share the garden.» Nobody was in a contest here. An adjudicator can also settle an official disagreement between people.
fact: An adjudicator is a person who judges a contest and decides who wins.
fact: You will often find adjudicators at music festivals, dance shows, drama contests and debating competitions.
fact: «Adjudicator» can also mean someone who officially decides a disagreement between people.
fact: If you are not sure of a word, swap in a meaning you know and check that the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: What is the job of an adjudicator? | *To judge a contest and decide who wins | To make the costumes | To sell the tickets | To sing the loudest
exercise: Where might you find an adjudicator? | In a supermarket queue | Inside a swimming pool | *At a school music festival | At the dentist's chair
exercise: Find the word in «The adjudicator wrote notes on each speech.» that names the person who judges. | notes | *adjudicator | speech | wrote
test: «Two brothers could not agree who owned the old bike, so an adjudicator was asked to decide.» What is an adjudicator in this sentence? | A bike shop worker | *A person who officially decides a disagreement | A rider in a race | A brother who wins
test: Which sentence uses adjudicator correctly? | The adjudicator sang the lead part in the school play | The adjudicator baked a cake for the contest | *The adjudicator listened to the debaters and decided who had argued best | The adjudicator was a sunny afternoon
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to adjudicator? | Spectator | *Judge | Competitor | Costume
